# Before writing or changing music, read music/README.md (style, moods, format).
# Not a song: a jingle, played once as a sound (like music/jingles/victory.scrim). For reaching the core (depth 20; docs/story.md), when the story goes in.
# Not played by the game yet: only in tools/player.html, under Jingles.
title    The Core
composer Claude
about    The glass bird glued back together: the toy tune whole again on crystal (A B C, E D), its last notes mended (B where the crack was, then A), over the title's rocking ostinato, glass harmonica chords, a singing bowl, and the bird's wide call ringing as at the end of the title song.
tempo    96
beats    2
steps    6
reverb   0.55

# mood explore: lead ost bird harm bass bowl chimes

voice lead     crystal    vol=0.78 pan=-0.1
voice ost      crystal    vol=0.38 pan=-0.3 oct=1
voice bird     crystal    vol=0.55 pan=0.4  rev=0.75
voice harm     glassharp  vol=0.26 pan=0.2  center=A4 att=0.2 rel=1.2
voice bass     fretless   vol=0.6
voice bowl     bowl       vol=0.4  pan=0.1  rev=0.6
voice chimes   chimes     vol=0.36 pan=-0.35

# Am F, E Am: the tune, mended
pattern mended
lead    | A4--- B4- C5----- | E5----- D5----- | B4----- A4----- |
ost     | A2!- A2- B2- A2!- A2- B2- | F2!- F2- G2- F2!- F2- G2- | E2!- E2- F2- A2!----- |
harm    | [Am]?----------- | [F]?----------- | [E]?----- [Am]----- |
bass    | C2----------- | A1----------- | G#1----- C2----- |
bowl    | A2----------- | _ | _ |
bird    | _ | _ | .----- A6 A5+B5---- |
chimes  | _ | _ | ...... x..x.. |

loop mended
